fireworks lit up the konya sky as  turkish president recep tayyip erdogan  inaugurated the islamic solidarity games  four thousand athletes from 56 muslim  majority countries are taking part in  the tournament  for 25 year old saudi weightlifter  anushahiri these games are very  important  unity  unity and getting to know each other  more and make a community of this sport  and other sports  it's anu's first international  competition  but there are more experienced athletes  as well  ahmed behalu's grandparents were forced  to leave their home in haifa israel  during the six day war of 1967.  they settled in the oscar refugee camp  in nablus in the occupied west bank  his parents were born and raised there  as was ahamad himself  a lifelong dream was realized when the  palestinian taekwondo federation started  ahmed fighting in 2018. since then the  20 year old has participated in seven  international competitions and won six  medals including one gold  the difficulties we face are tremendous  international travel is one of the main  problems as getting a permit from israel  authorities is not easy we have limited  resources and poor facilities to train  and prepare for the games but despite  these obstacles we have achieved great  success and in these games in kanye i  will do my best to win a gold medal  ahmed has also set his size on  representing palestine at the 2024  olympics in paris  [Applause]  the islamic solidarity games isn't a  high-profile competition but for many  young athletes it's an opportunity to  showcase their talents  millions of muslims have been suffering  from poverty political instability and  even civil wars for decades despite the  availability of tremendous human and  natural resources some say this is  because of a lack of unity solidarity  and coordination and the organizers of  this game say their aim is to build  bridges among the muslim majority  countries by bringing them together  through supports the suicide al jazeera  konya
 

